I went to see the elephants play;
  The young ones had been taught how to caper;
They pranced around and gambolled so gay!
 I saw one among them, very small indeed;
 It was hardly six inches high, but it could caper just as well as any big elephant could do,
 And that is what made me wonder and stare

THE evening wind had lost its sting,
 The day was done, the stars were bright;
 When suddenly, as though we heard
 An echo sounding through the night,
 There came an answering song!
 The moon had set and shadows crept
 In creeping, trembling tones, to speak
 Of other things than those they met;
 But soon a change appeared, that seemed
 To lift above the earth the dream
 Which hung on some tall poplar tree;
 It spoke, it sang, but words there were none;
